 "notes": "Flat/hilly stage Chambéry – Voiron, 174.7 km. Neutral start from the Fontaine des Éléphants in Chambéry north along Avenue/Route d'Aix-les-Bains (13:20); km 0 (départ réel) is on the Route d'Aix-les-Bains (D991 per hedgehog) just short of Viviers-du-Lac – placed at 45.6370,5.9124, about 1.7 km before the turn onto the Route du Lac; this position makes the routed distances to the Côte de Bassa (19.2), Côte de Rossillon (35.5) and Col des Prés (49.6) summits match the official km within 0.1 km, but the exact spot is not published (±1 km). Course: Viviers-du-Lac, Route du Lac to the lakeside road (Les Rives du Lac, Bord du Lac, Bd Jean Charcot) into Aix-les-Bains (Petit Port, Bd de Lattre de Tassigny, Av. Franklin Roosevelt, Av. de Saint-Simond, Route de Pont-Pierre), D911 Route des Bauges via Grésy-sur-Aix and the Côte de Bassa to Cusy, Pont de Banges, Lescheraines; D59 (Route de Rossillon – Côte de Rossillon, Route du Cimeterêt past Le Cimeterêt/Aillon-le-Vieux, Route sur la Vy) to Aillon-le-Jeune; D206 over the Col des Prés, Thoiry, Leysse bridge and the Côte de Saint-Jean-d'Arvey; D912 down to Saint-Alban-Leysse; Chambéry second passage (Route de Challes through the closed N201 interchange 18, Faubourg Montmélian, Av. Marius Berroir, rond-point J.-J. Rousseau, Rue André Jacques, Avenue de Lyon, Place Lucien Biset, Giratoire de la Favorite) and D1006 via Cognin, Saint-Thibaud-de-Couz, Col de Couz, Saint-Jean-de-Couz, Saint-Christophe-la-Grotte, Les Échelles, Gorges de Chailles, Saint-Béron to the D1006 roundabout at Le Pont-de-Beauvoisin; D82 over the Guiers into Isère (Av. des Trois Saints, Route des Éteppes, Route de la Chartreuse) to Saint-Albin-de-Vaulserre; Route de la Valdaine/Route de Saint-Bueil, Saint-Bueil, La Grand'Route, Route de Savoie, Saint-Geoire-en-Valdaine, Route de Chartreuse/Route de Saint-Geoire, Massieu, Route du Val d'Ainan, D1075 to Chirens; Route de Bonpertuis and Route de Rives to Charavines; Route de Vers Ars, Route des Plaines past Oyeu, the road beside the A48 and Route du Tram to the Colombe sprint (147.5); Le Grand-Lemps, Route du Vercors/Avenue de la Gare (Izeaux) to the D1085, Beaucroissant, Rives, Charnècles, Moirans (Av. Marius Chorot), D120 over the A48 to La Buisse, D1075 Avenue du Vercors/Avenue Abel Rossignol (uncategorised climb of La Commanderie, top ≈ km 171.9–172.4) and Route de Grenoble into Voiron; finale: left Bd Denfert-Rochereau, right Bd Franklin Roosevelt, left Av. François Mitterrand, right Cours Sénozan; finish line on Cours Sénozan in front of the church (400 m final straight; line placed 400 m after the last corner, medium). Km: routed distance on Overture roads (total 175.17 km), piecewise-scaled between official anchors: km 0, Bassa 19.2, Rossillon 35.5, Col des Prés 49.6 and Saint-Jean-d'Arvey 59.5 summits (located on the road with the Copernicus 30 m DEM: 479/686/1138/610 m), Col de Couz 84.0 (top of the D1006 at the St-Thibaud/St-Jean-de-Couz boundary), Saint-Béron 100.7, finish 174.7. The Colombe sprint (official km 147.5) is then placed at km 147.5 on Route du Tram ~1.4 km west of Colombe centre: with the sprint at the village centre the official 27.2 km from the sprint to the finish would be shorter than the straight-line chain through Le Grand-Lemps, Izeaux, Beaucroissant, Rives, Moirans and La Buisse, so the line must lie west of the centre (or the itinerary km is approximate) – medium. Official town km (Voiron magazine itinerary, re-paired with cyclingstage climb/sprint km) agree within 0.5 km at Pont de Banges, Lescheraines, Thoiry, Cognin, Saint-Thibaud, Les Échelles, Saint-Béron, Saint-Albin, Beaucroissant, Rives, La Buisse (those town points = high); other town points differ by 0.7–1.8 km, probably because the itinerary uses commune entries rather than centres (kept medium). LOW-CONFIDENCE stretches: (1) km 0–12: exact km 0 and the streets through Aix-les-Bains (official Viviers 1.2 / Aix 8.2 are 1.0–1.4 km earlier than on this route); (2) km 64–71: Chambéry second passage (street sequence reconstructed from closure notices: Avenue de Lyon + Lucien Biset closed, interchange 18 closed); (3) km 125–136: Chirens – Charavines via Route de Bonpertuis/Route de Rives chosen because it matches the official 6.6 km (the shorter Route de Clermont would be 4.5 km); (4) km 141–147: Oyeu – Colombe on the road beside the A48 (hedgehog: D17, D520 beside the motorway, D73a) – Overture has no road numbers here; (5) km 164–170: Moirans – D120 – La Buisse junction (D120 per hedgehog; the race may pass La Buisse village instead of the bypass, ±0.5 km). Overture roads here have almost no D-numbers; numbers given are from hedgehog/cyclingstage/Savoie closure orders (D911, D59, D206, D912, D1006) or Overture refs (D1006, D1085, D120). Legs flagged by the 60 % straight-line rule (km 54–59 and 62–64) are hairpin descents/climbs of the D206 and D912; extra points were added there. Points before km 17.7 are medium because their km depends on the uncertain km 0 position. [geodata G: Aix-les-Bains Petit Port: the point sat 40 m north of the turn onto the Avenue du Petit Port, so the route rode 50 m on and came back; moved to the junction] [geodata G: Saint-Alban-Leysse: the Avenue de Chambéry point sat 200 m east of where the Route de Plainpalais comes down onto it, so the route turned back east to it, crossed to the D1006 and came back west (a 1.3 km loop); moved to the junction, 0.6 km from the Plainpalais roundabout as in the itinerary (65.6 -> 66.2)]",
